BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:PA Day: Hands-On Dinosaur Fossils
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T153000
UID:6a0db39143b41b3d0067c488@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an opportunity to handle\, examine up close and di
 scuss nine real and replica fossils in this fascinating hands-on workshop.
  Participants will be entertained and educated\, not just about the fossil
 s themselves\, but the paleontological aspects that underpin them. Concept
 s include: evolution\, fossilization\, ‘The Tree of Life’ (phylogeny) 
 and — of course — dinosaurs!\nThis program is for ages 6-12. Registrat
 ion is required\n.\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0db39143b41b3d0067c488
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
